    "created_at": "2026-02-02T20:50:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-02T20:50:38Z",
    "body": "> I assume all: unset is mostly useful so that things like font and color inherit (so, undoing the UA rules that would apply to the button otherwise)\n\nYes, this is the reason. Here is where @dbaron first suggested this: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/6001193/comment/1dabaa79_26201aeb/\n\nI originally did this instead:\n```css\nselect:not(:-internal-list-box) > button:first-child {\n  display: contents;\n  font: inherit;\n  color: inherit;\n  background-color: transparent;\n}\n```\n\nMaybe it would make the most sense to just say that the button is rendered with base appearance in this case? That should make all of the inheritable propreties inherit instead of getting special UA values, right?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
